  "responseText": "{\"reviewedAffectedSlots\":[\"W046\",\"W092\"],\"findings\":[\"W046 (nnxyz nifty faces #58): Correctly composited over white canvas reveals a pale, luminous ground — not a dark surround. Large translucent grey circles read as soft, light-diffusing overlays against white, not as outward-pushing elements against darkness. The overall palette is pastel and pearlescent: lavender, pink, yellow-green, and warm grey tones dominate. The eye hollows are deep dark-red/maroon, which remain the densest, most opaque zones, but they sit within a face that is largely light-toned and open rather than compressed. The description of 'dark-red eye hollows pull inward while translucent circles push the surrounding space outward simultaneously' partially holds, but the framing of the work as belonging to a dark-ground dynamic is inaccurate — the ground is pale and the face is luminous. The transition description referencing 'muted lavender-grey palette' (attributed to W046 in the W124 transition) is also affected. The immediately preceding work is W101, whose pale gold glowing background and downward tilt are correctly described.\",\"W092 (nnxyz nifty faces #60): Correctly composited over white canvas confirms a white ground, not a pale ground with colour threads floating freely. The crimson borders are heavy and press inward from all four edges. The interior is densely layered with grey-brown tonal masses (swirling dark forms suggesting facial volumes), overlaid with blue, yellow-green, red, and black line-work. Two red rectangles are visible as anchors. The description of 'pale ground' is broadly correct — white shows through in areas — but 'yellow-green and blue threads pull outward' understates the density of the dark tonal underlayer. The grey-brown swirling masses are a significant visual element missing from the current description. The transition from W065 references 'sparse white lines on black' which is accurate for W065; the contrast with W092's filled surface remains valid but the characterisation of W092's ground needs to acknowledge the grey-brown tonal layer beneath the line-work.\"],\"membershipConcerns\":[\"W046 (nnxyz nifty faces #58): With correct compositing, the ground is pale and luminous rather than dark. This weakens its role in Chapter 0 ('Surface and Presence') as framed by the gallery question about bright marks against dark surroundings. However, the dark-red eye hollows against a pale, mark-dense surface still support a reading about legibility and surface complexity. A role can be grounded in visible features — the contrast between the luminous open ground and the dense maroon voids — so membership is defensible, but the framing requires adjustment.\"],\"corrections\":[{\"slot\":\"W046\",\"whyHere\":\"Dense overlapping lines in red, yellow, teal, and white layer across a pale, luminous ground; large translucent grey circles diffuse the space around the face while deep maroon eye hollows remain the only zones of concentrated darkness, pulling attention inward against the otherwise open, light-filled surface.\",\"transitionFromPrevious\":\"The previous work's pale gold glow and steady blue irises gave a clear, fixed focal point; here the ground is equally light but the eye positions become dark voids, and attention disperses across a surface of crossing colour rather than settling on any single feature.\"},{\"slot\":\"W092\",\"whyHere\":\"Crimson borders press inward from all four edges onto a white ground; beneath the crossing blue, yellow-green, and red line-work, grey-brown tonal masses swirl to suggest facial volumes, and two red rectangles hold position as the only stable anchors inside a surface of continuous layered agitation.\",\"transitionFromPrevious\":\"The previous work's sparse white lines on black gave the face room inside near-empty darkness; here the white ground is almost entirely covered — by tonal masses, crimson borders, and crossing colour threads — replacing emptiness with dense, competing accumulation.\"}],\"chapterCorrections\":[{\"index\":0,\"introduction\":\"Four faces where the form is still largely readable, but the surface already resists easy description — layered with marks, translucent overlays, or tonal depth that complicate what lies beneath. Backgrounds range from near-black to pale and luminous, but in each case the surface itself becomes the primary obstacle to easy reading.\"}]}",
